QuestGuidance.Register("en",317,{
[10113]="700431AE\n1\tDeliver the damaged furs to a collection box\030Collect damaged furs (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire damaged furs.\n",
[10114]="700431A8\n1\tDeliver the pitted sword sheaths to a collection box\030Collect pitted sword sheaths (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire pitted sword sheaths.\n",
[10115]="700431AA\n1\tDeliver the shattered hatchets to a collection box\030Collect shattered hatchets (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire shattered hatchets.\n",
[10116]="700431AB\n1\tDeliver the torn skins to a collection box\030Collect torn skins (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire torn skins.\n",
[10117]="700431AD\n1\tDeliver the toxic filth to a collection box\030Collect toxic filth (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire toxic filth.\n",
[10118]="7000A148\n1\tTalk to Calenglad\tThe Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir is north of Oatbarton along the road that runs through the Barandalf. Hal told you to follow the road north across the Brandywine until you reach a cross-roads and then to follow the westward road until you reach Tinnudir. Hal Gamgee has mentioned the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir in Lake Evendim and suggested that you speak to the Ranger Calenglad.\n",
[10119]="7000ACEC\n1\tPresent your Rangers' Cloaks to Techeron in Esteldín\030Craft Ranger's Cloaks (total: 5)\tTecheron is at Esteldín, in the North Downs. Techeron has asked you to weave some Rangers' cloaks for his kindred.\n",
[10120]="7000ACEA\n1\tPresent your Rangers' sashes to Techeron in Esteldín\030Craft Ranger's sashes (total: 5)\tTecheron is at Esteldín in the North Downs. Techeron has asked you to craft a number of Rangers' sashes for the youth of his kindred and bring them to him.\n",
[10121]="7000D4EF\n1\tUse Angmarim Banner (total: 5)\tThe banners of Angmar can be found in Bail Dílas, west of Gath Forthnír. Húriel asked you to enter Bail Dílas and remove the banners of Angmar, replacing them with the standards of the Dúnedain.\n2\tBring the banners of Angmar to Húriel at Gath Forthnír.\tHúriel is at Gath Forthnír, east of Bail Dílas. You have replaced all of Angmar's banners at Bail Dílas and should now return with them to Húriel.\n",
[10122]="7002672D\n1\tDefeat Angmarim in Haudh Arantar (total: 6)\tHaudh Arantar is south of the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings. Nethrandir asked you to go to Haudh Arantar and defeat the Angmarim within.\n2\tTalk to Nethrandir in the Way of Kings\tNethrandir is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings. Nethrandir will be pleased to hear Angmar has been sent a clear message.\n",
[10123]="7001B68F\n1\tRansacking Gathbúrz\t\n",
[10124]="7006C6FE\n1\tFind Raphûz near the boar camp west of Urmâkh\tRaphûz asks you to accompany him to find and defeat the boar Numûru tasked him with killing. The boar's lair is west from the settlement of Urmâkh.\n2\tComplete Instance: Raphûz's Challenge\tRaphûz was waiting near the boars outside of Urmâkh. He signaled to you and looks ready to find and defeat the target of his task from Numûru.\n3\tTalk to Raphûz\tYou assisted Raphûz in completing his task to face his fear and defeat the boar near Urmâkh. You should meet him at his home in Urmâkh to determine what to do next.\n",
[10125]="7006C6E5\n1\tFind Raphûz near the boar's den\tRaphûz told you he would make his way to the boar's camp and wait for you. Make your way to the east and find Raphûz outside of the boar camp.\n2\tComplete Instance: Facing His Fear\tRaphûz is prepared to enter the den and find the largest boar. Speak with him and see that he defeats the largest boar in Ambarûl.\n3\tTalk to Raphûz\tAfter defeating the boar, Urushagân, Raphûz told you he would speak to you about your efforts within the safety of Wrackwade.\n",
[10126]="7006C6F0\n1\tFind Raphûz near the scorpion nest near the salt mine\tRaphûz told you he would make his way to the scorpion nest north of Wrackwade to wait for you. Make your way to the north and find Raphûz outside of the salt mine.\n2\tComplete Instance: Proving His Bravery\tRaphûz is prepared to enter the nest to hunt the largest scorpion. Speak with him and see that he defeats the scorpion.\n3\tReturn to Wrackwade and speak with Raphûz\tRaphûz said he would meet you back in Wrackwade to discuss the defeat of the scorpion.\n",
[10127]="7002FCF4\n1\tCollect stolen rations from goblin riders (total: 8)\tGoblin riders near Garsfeld have stolen rations from the crofts. Gísling wants you to retrieve them and defeat the goblins that have burned the crofts of Garsfeld. Goblin riders can be found to the east and south-west of Garsfeld.\n2\tTalk to Gísling\tGísling can be found in the mead-hall of Garsfeld.\n",
[10128]="7006C4B4\n1\tSpeak with Enârshan when you are ready to defend her home\tOrcs have followed you back from Khûn Sagaz. Defeat them and protect Enârshan's home.\n2\tSpeak with Enârshan\tYou have defeated the Orcs who followed your tracks. Speak with Enârshan to ensure her that the threat is gone.\n",
[10129]="7007161F\n1\tCollect stolen rations (total: 12)\030Defeat Râhasham the Exiled\tThe brigands at Duríga have stolen food from the escapees at Dur Nâgu. You should reclaim the stolen rations and defeat the leader of the brigands, Râhasham the Exiled.\n2\tTalk to Kâbtam\tYou have reclaimed the stolen rations and defeated the brigand leader. You should return to Kâbtam in Dur Nâgu.\n",
[10130]="7006C52F\n1\tDefeat brigands in their encampment ([see journal]/16)\030Recover ration packs for Jirush ([see journal]/6)\030Recover the coffer of coins stolen from Jirush\tNisami explained that brigands, south-west beyond, raided Jirush and stole food and coin from the outpost. She asked you to go to the brigand encampment to recover the stolen goods and to avenge the people of Jirush.\n2\tDeliver the rations packs and coffer to Nisami in Jirush\tYou recovered the wealth and food for Jirush from the brigand camp south-west of Nirgambâr. Return the ration packs and the coffer to Nisami at Jirush in central Khûd Zagin.\n",
[10131]="70049420\n1\tDestroy supplies and collect rations at Dâr Mauzur\tSupplies and rations can be found at Dâr Mauzur. You should destroy supplies and collect rations.\n2\tDestroy supplies at Dâr Mauzur (total: 12)\030Collect rations at Dâr Mauzur (total: 10)\tSupplies and rations can be found at Dâr Mauzur. You should destroy supplies and collect rations.\n3\tBring the rations to Bregdal\tBregdal can be found on the border of Talath Úrui and Dor Amarth. You should speak with Bregdal.\n",
[10132]="7003EAFA\n1\tCollect boar-flanks on the High Moor (total: 6)\tBoars can be found throughout the High Moor, in the Trollshaws. Canaddal has asked you to hunt boars for meat to dry for rations.\n2\tBring the boar-flanks to Canaddal\tCanaddal is posted at the head of the path leading down to the Bruinen Gorges from the High Moor. You should bring the boar-flanks you collected to Canaddal.\n",
[10133]="70022BEE\n1\tFind the source of the rattling in the attic\tA strange rattling can be heard in the attic of the Haunted Burrow. You should seek out the source of the rattling and drive it off so that Polo can continue his search for treasure without troublesome interruptions.\n2\tReturn to Polo Puddifoot with news of the \"skeleton\"\tPolo Puddifoot awaits you outside the Haunted Burrow. You should return to Polo Puddifoot and tell him of this \"skeleton\" you encountered.\n",
[10134]="700082EC\n1\tCollect the helms of the fallen (total: 6)\tThe Orcs make their camp in the ravaged lands of Dol Dínen, far to the south-east of Esteldín. Not every traveller or resident of the North Downs has your good fortune and skill. Some have fallen to sword or spear of the twisted Orc-hordes. You should hunt Orcs in the ravaged lands and reclaim the helms of the fallen. NOTE: This is a fellowship quest.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have assisted the Rangers of Esteldín in their daily vigilance, maintaining that the lands of the North Downs are free from enemy control.\n",
[10135]="7000E39A\n1\tCollect moose-antlers (total: 10)\030Collect sinew (total: 10)\030Collect driftwood (total: 10)\tMoose-antlers can be gathered from the moose in the forests surrounding Kauppa-kohta. Sinew can be gathered from wolverines in the forests, and driftwood can be found along the southern shore of the lake. Eija has asked you to collect moose-antlers, sinew, and driftwood for use in crafting her sleds.\n2\tBring the materials to Eija\tEija is on the lakeshore in Kauppa-kohta. Now that you have collected the materials Eija requested, you should return to her.\n",
[10136]="7001BE3D\n1\tDefeat enemies at Bolg Maufulug (total: 6)\tBolg Maufulug lies west and a little north from Talan Fanuidhol. Caredwen has asked you to attack Bolg Maufulug and defeat any enemies you find there.\n2\tTalk to Caredwen at Talan Fanuidhol\tCaredwen is at Talan Fanuidhol, east and a little south of Bolg Maufulug. You should return to Caredwen with the tidings of your victory at Bolg Maufulug.\n",
[10137]="7001BE3E\n1\tDefeat enemies at Drûmaudhul (total: 15)\tDrûmaudhul lies to the north-west from Talan Gwilith. Belegoth has asked you to attack Drûmaudhul and defeat any enemies you find there.\n2\tTalk to Belegoth at Talan Gwilith\tBelegoth is at Talan Gwilith, south-east of Drûmaudhul. You should return to Belegoth with the tidings of your victory at Drûmaudhul.\n",
[10138]="7001BE41\n1\tDefeat enemies at Mokûrz Gundul (total: 6)\tMokûrz Gundul lies to the north from Talan Fanuidhol. Caredwen has asked you to attack Mokûrz Gundul and defeat any enemies you find there.\n2\tTalk to Caredwen at Talan Fanuidhol\tCaredwen is at Talan Fanuidhol, south of Mokûrz Gundul. You should return to Caredwen with the tidings of your victory at Mokûrz Gundul.\n",
[10139]="7001BE42\n1\tDefeat enemies at Nardur-stazg (total: 6)\tNardur-stazg lies to the north-west from Talan Gwilith. Belegoth has asked you to attack Nardur-stazg and defeat any enemies you find there.\n2\tTalk to Belegoth at Talan Gwilith\tBelegoth is at Talan Gwilith, south-east of Nardur-stazg. You should return to Belegoth with the tidings of your victory at Nardur-stazg.\n",
[10140]="70054682\n1\tReplace the broken Gilgelair (total: 7)\tBroken Gilgelair can be found inside Torech Ungol. You should replace the broken Gilgelair.\n2\tTalk to Celeborn\tCeleborn can be found outside Torech Ungol, at the top of the Winding Stair. You should inform Celeborn you have replaced the Gilgelair.\n",
[10141]="7002F064\n1\tCollect the purse of gold from the Orc that stole it\tThe distinctive scavenging Orc is probably lurking south-east of the Dead Orc Glade, in the East Wall. The wounded Uruk believes the scavenging Orc would seek higher ground. The wounded Uruk in the Dead Orc Glade has promised to tell you what happened there... once you recover the purse of gold that was stolen by an Orc.\n2\tBring purse of gold to the wounded Uruk\tThe wounded Uruk in the Dead Orc Glade is waiting for you to return his stolen purse of gold.\n",
[10142]="70015E33\n1\tTalk to Palanaer at Echad Dúnann\tPalanaer is at Echad Dúnann, south-east of Echad Eregion. Ladenthir has asked you to bear news of Saruman's encroachment upon Eregion to Palanaer, another of the scouts of Rivendell.\n",
[10143]="7005A653\n1\tLook out into the Deepscrave\030Destroy Orc warning totems in Máttugard (total: 10)\030Look down into the Deepscrave\tThe overlook to Deepscrave can be found in the southern edge of Máttugard. You should scout the edges of Máttugard and destroy any Orc warning totems that you find.\n2\tTalk to Hetbrúda near Deepscrave in Máttugard\tHetbrúda can be found near the entrance to Deepscrave in Máttugard. You should talk to Hetbrúda.\n",
[10144]="7001750B\n1\tCollect a water sample\030Find a likely place from which to draw water\tWater samples can be drawn from the water's edge north-east from the entrance to the Vile Maw. Kaldi said that since he heard the noises near the Vile Maw, he has not been down to the water. He asked you to make your way there to take a sample for him and provided you with an empty phial.\n2\tBring the sample to Kaldi outside the Vile Maw\030Collect Water-sample\tKaldi is at his little camp outside the Vile Maw. You should bring the water sample you collected to Kaldi.\n",
})
